\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The challenge has been linked to the death of several children, including a mere 10 and 12-year-old./34 These challenges not only make the videos go viral, but the kids and teens that engage in them are rewarded with positive feedback. They gain likes, followers, and comments that makes them want to keep engaging in them and encourages others to follow suit.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Because of the anonymity the internet and social media offers, it has also become easier than ever to run into sexual abuse, harassment, and hate speech. Kids face an alarming amount of sexual encounters and sexual abuse online. One in four kids between the age of 9 and 17 reported having a sexual encounter with someone they believed to be an adult on social media./35 A study found 8 in 10 tweens and teens reported witnessing or experiencing bullying in 2020, and 9 in 10 witnessed violent subject matter./36 In 55 percent of cases where a child blocked an aggressor, the aggressors quickly found the child again through creating a new account or going on another platform./37 The percentage of teens who see racist content has also nearly doubled in the past two years./38 Hate speech already targets vulnerable groups by race, gender, and sexual orientation, and it exacerbates negative mental health outcomes.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Finally, algorithms also contribute to spreading misinformation and disinformation. Our research shows that 77 percent of teens get their news from social media, and 39 percent of their news from influencers and celebrities./39 Yet during the election season, platforms are often not fact-checking political content, labeling, demoting, or removing false or misleading posts, or removing hate speech and voter suppression content.40 This could cause irreparable damage to our democracy, because teens are turning to these sources for valuable information as they get ready to participate in our democracy and civic activities such as voting.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Teens, and particularly teen girls, are helpless against a social media machine that is powered by algorithms that deliberately amplify hate, misinformation, and feeds images to teens of perfectly shaped individuals who they then compare themselves to as the standard of beauty.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 III. Platforms Are Filled With and Promote Overly Commercial Content}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0
